# ==============================================================================
# .chezmoiremove.tmpl
# ==============================================================================
# STATUS: intentionally inert. Every line below is commented out, including the
#   template directives, so this file currently removes nothing. It is kept as
#   a working reference for the syntax should a purge ever be needed. Do not
#   delete it for "doing nothing" — that is deliberate.
#
# Purpose:
#   Defines files, directories, or patterns relative to $HOME that chezmoi
#   must ensure DO NOT exist on the target system.
#
# Behavior:
#   - Paths listed here are deleted from $HOME during 'chezmoi apply'.
#   - Supports Go template logic to conditionally purge GUI/desktop artifacts
#     when transitioning or deploying to headless or container environments.
#   - Paths must be relative to $HOME (e.g., .config/app/config.json).
#
# Note on scope:
#   Preventing GUI configs from being *deployed* to headless machines is
#   handled by .chezmoiignore, not here. This file would only be needed to
#   delete files already present in $HOME — for example on a machine that was
#   provisioned with a GUI and later switched to headless. Be deliberate: these
#   paths are removed on every apply.
# ==============================================================================

